  "description": {
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Strelitzia alba",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strelitzia_alba",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1341344277,
      "text": "Strelitzia alba also known as white-flowered wild banana, white bird of paradise, or Cape wild banana is a plant of the Bird of Paradise family and is endemic to the Garden Route along the southernmost coastal regions of the district of Humansdorp Eastern and district of Knysna in Western Cape in South Africa. It grows in evergreen forest, gorges, and on slopes along the rivers."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Strelitzia alba",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strelitzia_alba",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 174022239,
      "text": "Strelitzia alba, también conocida como ave del paraíso blanca o ave del paraíso del Cabo, es una planta de la familia Strelitziaceae, endémica de Garden Route a lo largo de las regiones costeras más meridionales del distrito de Humansdorp Eastern y el distrito de Knysna en Western Cape en Sudáfrica. Crece en bosques de hoja perenne, desfiladeros y en laderas a lo largo de los ríos."
    }
  },
